                <pb facs="0397" n="269" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg269"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 209.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr.
                            Becerra</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 1,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your note
                    of the 27th ultimo, in regard to the brig Ambrose Light, recently captured by
                    the U. S. S. Alliance in the Caribbean Sea, and have transmitted a copy of your
                    note to the honorable A. H. Garland, Attorney-General, for his consideration and
                    action.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
